WEBVTT

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:04.422
♪ It seems today

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:04.422
that all you see ♪

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:07.592
♪ Is violence in movies

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:07.592
and sex on TV ♪

00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:11.262
♪ But where are those

00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:11.262
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:00:11.303 --> 00:00:14.265
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:17.643
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:00:17.685 --> 00:00:21.272
♪ Lucky there's a man

00:00:17.685 --> 00:00:21.272
who positively can do ♪

00:00:21.313 --> 00:00:22.481
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:23.608
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:29.614
♪ He's... a...

00:00:23.649 --> 00:00:29.614
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:36.621
Oh, Stewie,

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:36.621
how exciting!

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:38.873
Your first visit to

00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:38.873
a real fire station!

00:00:38.915 --> 00:00:41.876
Yeah, you kids always loved your

00:00:38.915 --> 00:00:41.876
first trip to the fire station.

00:00:41.918 --> 00:00:43.502
You remember when we took Meg?

00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:49.675
Welcome to the Quahog

00:00:47.465 --> 00:00:49.675
Fire Department, folks.

00:00:49.717 --> 00:00:51.343
I'm Captain Beckman.

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:52.177
Let me know if you

00:00:51.385 --> 00:00:52.177
have any questions

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:53.638
that I can

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:53.638
answer for you.

00:00:53.679 --> 00:00:55.180
JOE:

00:00:53.679 --> 00:00:55.180
What's up, nerds?

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:58.476
You waiting for some guy to

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:58.476
fall asleep with a cigarette?

00:00:58.517 --> 00:00:59.685
Lazy fire turds!

00:00:59.727 --> 00:01:01.479
Have another donut, pig!

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.439
We got guns! You got hoses!

00:01:03.481 --> 00:01:05.524
See you on the softball field!

00:01:10.571 --> 00:01:13.616
Over here is our kitchen,

00:01:10.571 --> 00:01:13.616
where we make all our meals.

00:01:13.658 --> 00:01:15.618
And upstairs

00:01:13.658 --> 00:01:15.618
is where we sleep.

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.077
What about your

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.077
wives and families?

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:19.956
Sometimes we don't see them

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:19.956
for long periods of time.

00:01:19.998 --> 00:01:21.833
Well, that sounds

00:01:19.998 --> 00:01:21.833
awfully lonely.

00:01:21.874 --> 00:01:24.335
Like being an NBA player

00:01:21.874 --> 00:01:24.335
on the road.

00:01:24.376 --> 00:01:26.420
Baby, I miss my wife so much.

00:01:26.462 --> 00:01:28.464
Thanks for understanding

00:01:26.462 --> 00:01:28.464
that we can't do anything.

00:01:28.506 --> 00:01:29.465
I just want to cuddle.

00:01:29.507 --> 00:01:31.050
Oh, you're so sweet.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.677
I'm just doing

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:32.677
what a man should do.

00:01:32.718 --> 00:01:35.429
Respecting the sacred

00:01:32.718 --> 00:01:35.429
institution of marriage.

00:01:35.471 --> 00:01:37.515
And now, straight to sleep.

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.892
ANNOUNCER:

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.892
This message brought

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:39.892
to you by the NBA.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:41.393
Let's all pretend this happens.

00:01:41.435 --> 00:01:44.355
Hey, Chris, you think it's safe

00:01:41.435 --> 00:01:44.355
to drink from a fire hose?

00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:45.690
Why not, Dad?

00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:45.690
It's just water.

00:01:45.731 --> 00:01:48.067
All right, well, turn it on.

00:01:45.731 --> 00:01:48.067
I'm very thirsty.

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:51.737
Nice job, Chris.

00:01:51.779 --> 00:01:53.155
You got my shirt wet.

00:01:53.197 --> 00:01:54.198
Now, few people realize

00:01:54.239 --> 00:01:57.368
that until 1928

00:01:54.239 --> 00:01:57.368
there were no hoses,

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:00.496
and you actually had to fight

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:00.496
fires with your bare hands.

00:02:00.538 --> 00:02:02.498
I will now give

00:02:00.538 --> 00:02:02.498
a demonstration.

00:02:07.461 --> 00:02:08.546
(grunts)

00:02:10.589 --> 00:02:12.591
Whoa, scrappy little blaze, huh?

00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:14.719
Oh, my God,

00:02:12.633 --> 00:02:14.719
the fire's got a gun!

00:02:17.555 --> 00:02:19.348
What the (bleep) was that?

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:21.475
(making driving noises)

00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:24.020
Come on, Stewie.

00:02:22.768 --> 00:02:24.020
We're going.

00:02:24.062 --> 00:02:25.437
Just a moment, Brian.

00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:26.731
I'm pretending

00:02:25.479 --> 00:02:26.731
I'm a fireman.

00:02:26.772 --> 00:02:28.524
I love playing pretend.

00:02:28.566 --> 00:02:30.985
My name's Peter

00:02:28.566 --> 00:02:30.985
and I work in the brewery.

00:02:31.027 --> 00:02:32.528
Now I'm gonna put on my pants

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:33.905
and go talk

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:33.905
to my coworkers at...

00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:35.740
These pants have

00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:35.740
stool in them.

00:02:39.618 --> 00:02:42.580
Well, I hope everyone had a fun

00:02:39.618 --> 00:02:42.580
afternoon at the firehouse.

00:02:42.621 --> 00:02:44.456
I sure did, Mom!

00:02:44.498 --> 00:02:47.543
I can't wait for the

00:02:44.498 --> 00:02:47.543
next family outing!

00:02:49.545 --> 00:02:50.838
Aw, thanks, Mike.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.590
I hate fire stations.

00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:54.425
(man's voice):

00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:54.425
No problem, man.

00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:54.425
(sniffing)

00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:56.427
Is that alcohol

00:02:54.466 --> 00:02:56.427
on your breath?

00:02:56.468 --> 00:02:57.720
Yeah, maybe.

00:02:57.762 --> 00:03:00.347
You're playing this

00:02:57.762 --> 00:03:00.347
too fast and loose, Mike!

00:03:04.602 --> 00:03:05.770
Ooh, ooh, is

00:03:04.602 --> 00:03:05.770
that the mail?

00:03:05.811 --> 00:03:07.563
Yeah.

00:03:05.811 --> 00:03:07.563
Is there anything

00:03:05.811 --> 00:03:07.563
in there for me?

00:03:07.605 --> 00:03:08.773
I want to see if

00:03:07.605 --> 00:03:08.773
there's a response

00:03:08.814 --> 00:03:10.733
to all those fan letters

00:03:08.814 --> 00:03:10.733
I've been writing.

00:03:10.775 --> 00:03:12.777
PETER:

00:03:10.775 --> 00:03:12.777
Dear Cary Elwes,

00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:15.571
I have been meaning to

00:03:12.818 --> 00:03:15.571
contact you for some time.

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:18.657
I have never been able to

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:18.657
figure out if you are famous.

00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:20.659
You were a big deal

00:03:18.699 --> 00:03:20.659
in one thing,

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.454
but you were wearing

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:23.454
a mask for most of it.

00:03:23.495 --> 00:03:25.831
Do you consider your

00:03:23.495 --> 00:03:25.831
career a disappointment?

00:03:25.873 --> 00:03:28.584
Or rather, did you exceed

00:03:25.873 --> 00:03:28.584
your own expectations?

00:03:28.626 --> 00:03:30.962
Yours truly, Peter Griffin.

00:03:31.003 --> 00:03:34.423
P.S. You were in

00:03:31.003 --> 00:03:34.423
Robin Hood: Men in Tights.

00:03:34.465 --> 00:03:36.258
Did you know that?

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.552
Hey, there's something here

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.552
from the Nielsen Company.

00:03:39.511 --> 00:03:40.888
"Dear Griffin family,

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.891
"You have been specially

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.891
selected from amongst millions

00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:46.769
"of American households

00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:46.769
to be a Nielsen family,

00:03:46.811 --> 00:03:50.439
"and as such, to have your

00:03:46.811 --> 00:03:50.439
TV viewing habits monitored

00:03:50.481 --> 00:03:53.651
in order to measure

00:03:50.481 --> 00:03:53.651
television ratings."

00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:56.695
Oh, kids, this came

00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:56.695
all the way from Delaware.

00:03:56.737 --> 00:03:58.114
What does all

00:03:56.737 --> 00:03:58.114
that mean?

00:03:58.156 --> 00:04:00.658
Well, Meg, it sounds like

00:03:58.156 --> 00:04:00.658
they want us to be part of

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:02.827
a select group of people that

00:04:00.699 --> 00:04:02.827
helps determine what's on TV.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:04.495
We're gonna be a Nielsen family?

00:04:04.536 --> 00:04:05.287
That's awesome!

00:04:05.329 --> 00:04:07.623
(somber, sad music plays)

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.626
I think... uh...

00:04:10.668 --> 00:04:12.211
I think that's

00:04:10.668 --> 00:04:12.211
the wrong music.

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:14.797
(victorious fanfare plays)

00:04:14.839 --> 00:04:16.590
There you go.

00:04:23.681 --> 00:04:26.809
Now, this Nielsen box will keep

00:04:23.681 --> 00:04:26.809
track of everything you watch,

00:04:26.851 --> 00:04:29.061
which helps us generalize

00:04:26.851 --> 00:04:29.061
the viewing habits

00:04:29.103 --> 00:04:30.646
of millions of Americans.

00:04:30.688 --> 00:04:32.106
Ah, yes.

00:04:32.148 --> 00:04:34.150
And what was that beginning,

00:04:32.148 --> 00:04:34.150
middle and end part again?

00:04:34.192 --> 00:04:35.567
Um...

00:04:35.609 --> 00:04:38.612
this Nielsen box will keep track

00:04:35.609 --> 00:04:38.612
of everything you watch,

00:04:38.654 --> 00:04:40.823
which helps us generalize

00:04:38.654 --> 00:04:40.823
the viewing habits

00:04:40.865 --> 00:04:42.700
of millions of Americans.

00:04:42.741 --> 00:04:44.535
Is there any way you can

00:04:42.741 --> 00:04:44.535
describe that to me

00:04:44.576 --> 00:04:46.078
using colorful puppets

00:04:44.576 --> 00:04:46.078
of some sort?

00:04:47.913 --> 00:04:51.500
The Nielsen box will monitor

00:04:47.913 --> 00:04:51.500
your viewing habits!

00:04:51.542 --> 00:04:52.835
(scratchy laugh)

00:04:52.877 --> 00:04:56.463
I don't like the left puppet.

00:04:52.877 --> 00:04:56.463
His chin is scary.

00:04:57.882 --> 00:04:59.717
Well, thanks

00:04:57.882 --> 00:04:59.717
for your cooperation.

00:04:59.758 --> 00:05:01.844
If you have any questions,

00:04:59.758 --> 00:05:01.844
please call me.

00:05:01.886 --> 00:05:03.721
And welcome

00:05:01.886 --> 00:05:03.721
to the Nielsen family.

00:05:03.762 --> 00:05:06.265
Thank you very much.

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.933
Well, isn't this exciting.

00:05:07.975 --> 00:05:09.894
I know, I can't believe

00:05:07.975 --> 00:05:09.894
we're a Nielsen family!

00:05:09.935 --> 00:05:11.854
I never get picked

00:05:09.935 --> 00:05:11.854
for anything.

00:05:15.816 --> 00:05:18.027
(people screaming)

00:05:28.579 --> 00:05:29.454
All right, everyone.

00:05:29.496 --> 00:05:30.956
Time to do

00:05:29.496 --> 00:05:30.956
our Nielsen duty.

00:05:30.998 --> 00:05:32.624
So, what are we gonna watch?

00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:33.959
Boobs!

00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:33.959
Project Runway!

00:05:34.001 --> 00:05:36.087
The Good Wife!

00:05:34.001 --> 00:05:36.087
That black version

00:05:34.001 --> 00:05:36.087
of our show!

00:05:36.128 --> 00:05:38.005
You know, guys, this

00:05:36.128 --> 00:05:38.005
is a real opportunity

00:05:38.047 --> 00:05:39.673
to promote quality

00:05:38.047 --> 00:05:39.673
programming.

00:05:39.715 --> 00:05:40.841
I think we should

00:05:39.715 --> 00:05:40.841
watch PBS.

00:05:40.883 --> 00:05:42.927
Yeah, you're real

00:05:40.883 --> 00:05:42.927
passionate about PBS.

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:46.097
You donated once five years ago

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:46.097
and they sent you a mug.

00:05:46.138 --> 00:05:48.724
And now the mug's so old

00:05:46.138 --> 00:05:48.724
that the "P" has been worn off

00:05:48.766 --> 00:05:50.142
so it just says "B.S."

00:05:50.184 --> 00:05:52.811
It's libtards like you that are

00:05:50.184 --> 00:05:52.811
screwing up our country.

00:05:52.853 --> 00:05:55.773
(knock at door)

00:05:55.814 --> 00:05:57.608
Tom Tucker?

00:05:55.814 --> 00:05:57.608
What are you doing here?

00:05:57.649 --> 00:05:59.026
Well, I heard you're

00:05:57.649 --> 00:05:59.026
the new Nielsen family.

00:05:59.068 --> 00:06:01.653
Just hoping you plan to watch

00:05:59.068 --> 00:06:01.653
the Channel Five News.

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:03.155
I don't know.

00:06:01.695 --> 00:06:03.155
I've missed so many.

00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:04.740
It's gonna take me

00:06:03.197 --> 00:06:04.740
forever to catch up.

00:06:04.782 --> 00:06:06.992
Well, we'd sure love

00:06:04.782 --> 00:06:06.992
to have you as a viewer.

00:06:07.034 --> 00:06:08.286
Is there anything we can do

00:06:08.327 --> 00:06:10.621
to make the news

00:06:08.327 --> 00:06:10.621
more appealing to you?

00:06:08.327 --> 00:06:10.621
Maybe.

00:06:10.662 --> 00:06:12.206
I guess you could

00:06:10.662 --> 00:06:12.206
lose the moustache.

00:06:12.248 --> 00:06:13.582
Lose my moustache?

00:06:13.624 --> 00:06:15.584
Well, gosh, I...

00:06:13.624 --> 00:06:15.584
I don't know.

00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:16.752
My birthmark

00:06:15.626 --> 00:06:16.752
makes it kind of tough.

00:06:16.794 --> 00:06:19.421
Always caused me problems

00:06:16.794 --> 00:06:19.421
at my old job.

00:06:19.463 --> 00:06:21.966
And that'll do it for us here

00:06:19.463 --> 00:06:21.966
at Channel 12 News.

00:06:22.007 --> 00:06:23.592
Make sure you turn

00:06:22.007 --> 00:06:23.592
those clocks ahead.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:24.843
Good night, St. Louis.

00:06:24.885 --> 00:06:26.053
Yeah, I don't know,

00:06:26.095 --> 00:06:27.554
I was never that crazy

00:06:26.095 --> 00:06:27.554
about the moustache.

00:06:27.596 --> 00:06:29.848
Well, I suppose I could lose it

00:06:27.596 --> 00:06:29.848
and just use more makeup.

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:31.350
Yeah, that'd be cool.

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.644
And maybe a festive hat would

00:06:31.391 --> 00:06:33.644
make things more festive.

00:06:33.685 --> 00:06:35.854
All right, this is good.

00:06:33.685 --> 00:06:35.854
Any other suggestions?

00:06:35.896 --> 00:06:37.106
Yeah, can you end each show

00:06:37.148 --> 00:06:39.942
by trying to pull-start

00:06:37.148 --> 00:06:39.942
a very cold chain saw?

00:06:39.984 --> 00:06:41.110
Well, that shouldn't

00:06:39.984 --> 00:06:41.110
be a problem.

00:06:41.152 --> 00:06:42.820
All right, thank you

00:06:41.152 --> 00:06:42.820
for being so candid.

00:06:42.861 --> 00:06:43.988
Hey, thanks for listening.

00:06:44.029 --> 00:06:45.990
I know how hard it is

00:06:44.029 --> 00:06:45.990
to take criticism.

00:06:46.907 --> 00:06:48.075
Hey, nice boots, Griffin.

00:06:48.117 --> 00:06:50.661
They sell men's shoes

00:06:48.117 --> 00:06:50.661
where you got those?

00:06:50.702 --> 00:06:52.621
PETER:

00:06:50.702 --> 00:06:52.621
You made a commitment

00:06:50.702 --> 00:06:52.621
to these boots, Peter.

00:06:52.663 --> 00:06:54.039
These boots are the new you,

00:06:54.081 --> 00:06:55.833
and no one will shake that.

00:06:55.874 --> 00:06:58.210
Yee-haw, ride 'em, cowgirl!

00:06:58.252 --> 00:07:00.004
PETER:

00:06:58.252 --> 00:07:00.004
Okay, you can take

00:06:58.252 --> 00:07:00.004
the boots off at lunch.

00:07:00.045 --> 00:07:01.880
Go to the gym.

00:07:00.045 --> 00:07:01.880
Have a workout.

00:07:01.922 --> 00:07:03.341
Come back in your sneakers.

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:05.467
If anyone asks, you forgot

00:07:03.382 --> 00:07:05.467
the boots in your locker.

00:07:05.509 --> 00:07:07.011
Just make it to lunch.

00:07:07.052 --> 00:07:08.762
Those boots are

00:07:07.052 --> 00:07:08.762
made for walkin'.

00:07:08.804 --> 00:07:10.181
Up to guys' butts.

00:07:10.222 --> 00:07:12.391
(laughing)

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.310
Hey, fellas.

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.310
Hey.

00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:18.814
TOM TUCKER:

00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:18.814
Good evening, Quahog.

00:07:18.856 --> 00:07:20.649
Tonight, Channel Five

00:07:18.856 --> 00:07:20.649
mourns the loss

00:07:20.691 --> 00:07:21.900
of a dear colleague.

00:07:21.942 --> 00:07:23.402
My moustache.

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.863
And as per the wishes

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.863
of my moustache,

00:07:25.904 --> 00:07:28.199
his ashes were sprinkled

00:07:25.904 --> 00:07:28.199
off the coast of Acapulco

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.408
where he was born.

00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.076
Well, that'll do it for us here.

00:07:31.118 --> 00:07:32.411
Thanks for watching

00:07:31.118 --> 00:07:32.411
Channel Five,

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:34.621
the most trusted name in news.

00:07:37.041 --> 00:07:38.917
Ah, crap.

00:07:38.959 --> 00:07:41.170
Oh, come on.

00:07:43.047 --> 00:07:45.007
Let's go, Tom.

00:07:45.049 --> 00:07:46.675
Work, damn it!

00:07:46.717 --> 00:07:47.592
What the hell?

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:48.886
What's going on

00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:48.886
with the news?

00:07:48.927 --> 00:07:51.305
This is terrible!

00:07:48.927 --> 00:07:51.305
Yeah, has he lost his mind?

00:07:51.347 --> 00:07:52.723
Well, I'll be damned.

00:07:52.764 --> 00:07:55.100
If I knew he was gonna do

00:07:52.764 --> 00:07:55.100
all that stuff I told him,

00:07:55.142 --> 00:07:56.268
I would've told him

00:07:55.142 --> 00:07:56.268
more stuff.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:57.311
What?

00:07:57.353 --> 00:07:59.521
