00:15:29.179 --> 00:15:30.138
Hello?

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:32.098
Ah, Hartman!

00:15:36.561 --> 00:15:37.813
Hey, guys.

00:15:36.561 --> 00:15:37.813
How you doing?

00:15:37.855 --> 00:15:38.897
Not so good, Peter.

00:15:38.938 --> 00:15:40.023
Yeah, me, either.

00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:42.359
Thanks to you,

00:15:40.064 --> 00:15:42.359
TV's a vast wasteland.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:43.360
You know how

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:43.360
I know that phrase?

00:15:43.401 --> 00:15:44.486
I read it in a book,

00:15:43.401 --> 00:15:44.486
you monster!

00:15:44.528 --> 00:15:46.363
Aw, come on, let me

00:15:44.528 --> 00:15:46.363
make it up to you.

00:15:46.404 --> 00:15:47.364
Let me buy you a beer.

00:15:47.405 --> 00:15:49.324
No, that seat's taken.

00:15:49.366 --> 00:15:50.200
Move along, Peter.

00:15:50.241 --> 00:15:51.827
What are you

00:15:50.241 --> 00:15:51.827
talking about?

00:15:51.869 --> 00:15:52.911
You guys are my pals.

00:15:52.952 --> 00:15:54.245
We used to be, Peter.

00:15:54.287 --> 00:15:55.246
Now, scram.

00:15:55.288 --> 00:15:57.207
Well, fine,

00:15:55.288 --> 00:15:57.207
I'll sit at the bar.

00:15:57.248 --> 00:15:58.917
Not at my bar, you won't.

00:15:58.958 --> 00:16:00.001
Get out of here!

00:16:00.043 --> 00:16:02.379
Geez, I can't

00:16:00.043 --> 00:16:02.379
show my face anywhere.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:05.173
I might as well be back

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:05.173
doing public radio.

00:16:05.215 --> 00:16:06.383
This is Peter Griffin,

00:16:06.424 --> 00:16:09.761
and you're listening

00:16:06.424 --> 00:16:09.761
to  Book Talk on WRNI.

00:16:09.803 --> 00:16:11.388
Today we'll be discussing

00:16:11.429 --> 00:16:12.639
Bret Easton Ellis's

00:16:11.429 --> 00:16:12.639
popular work,

00:16:12.681 --> 00:16:16.560
Less Than Zero, a tale

00:16:12.681 --> 00:16:16.560
of privilege, detachment

00:16:16.601 --> 00:16:18.770
and youthful alienation.

00:16:18.812 --> 00:16:20.772
(taking a long, loud sip of tea)

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.275
But first,

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.275
a word from our sponsor,

00:16:24.317 --> 00:16:26.194
Westin's Golden Soda Biscuits.

00:16:26.236 --> 00:16:28.196
I'm enjoying one right now.

00:16:28.238 --> 00:16:30.407
(crunches biscuit)

00:16:30.448 --> 00:16:31.575
Mmm.

00:16:31.616 --> 00:16:35.412
(sips, then crunches)

00:16:35.453 --> 00:16:37.372
Mmm.

00:16:37.414 --> 00:16:40.584
(sips tea, crunches biscuit)

00:16:40.625 --> 00:16:42.377
Mmm.

00:16:42.419 --> 00:16:45.964
(sips tea, crunches biscuit)

00:16:48.926 --> 00:16:50.385
(sips tea)

00:16:50.427 --> 00:16:52.596
Mmm.

00:16:56.266 --> 00:16:58.435
That concludes

00:16:56.266 --> 00:16:58.435
today's session of  Book Talk.

00:16:58.476 --> 00:17:01.396
Tune in tomorrow when we will

00:16:58.476 --> 00:17:01.396
look at John Kennedy Toole's

00:17:01.438 --> 00:17:04.274
unheralded early work,

00:17:01.438 --> 00:17:04.274
The Neon Bible.

00:17:08.403 --> 00:17:09.654
Hey, what's wrong, Peter?

00:17:09.696 --> 00:17:10.989
I miss my friends, Brian.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.408
I mean, I was having fun

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:13.408
with those Nielsen boxes,

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.452
but what's the point

00:17:15.493 --> 00:17:17.704
if I don't got Joe and

00:17:15.493 --> 00:17:17.704
Quagmire to enjoy it with me?

00:17:17.746 --> 00:17:20.498
I guess I shouldn't have

00:17:17.746 --> 00:17:20.498
messed with television.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.417
Well, it's not

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.417
exactly your fault.

00:17:22.459 --> 00:17:24.043
The networks never should

00:17:22.459 --> 00:17:24.043
have listened to you

00:17:24.085 --> 00:17:25.253
in the first place.

00:17:25.295 --> 00:17:26.463
This is exactly what

00:17:25.295 --> 00:17:26.463
makes bad television:

00:17:26.504 --> 00:17:28.840
pandering to the lowest

00:17:26.504 --> 00:17:28.840
common denominator.

00:17:28.882 --> 00:17:30.383
So what do I do, Brian?

00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:31.969
Well, you still

00:17:30.425 --> 00:17:31.969
have these boxes.

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.846
That means you still have the

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:34.846
power to influence television.

00:17:34.888 --> 00:17:37.015
Maybe you can use that

00:17:34.888 --> 00:17:37.015
power to help restore TV

00:17:37.056 --> 00:17:38.433
to the way it was.

00:17:38.475 --> 00:17:39.517
You're right, Brian.

00:17:39.559 --> 00:17:40.894
Maybe if I watch

00:17:39.559 --> 00:17:40.894
smart, quality shows,

00:17:40.936 --> 00:17:43.104
that'll help get things back

00:17:40.936 --> 00:17:43.104
to the way they were.

00:17:43.146 --> 00:17:45.440
We can use these boxes

00:17:43.146 --> 00:17:45.440
for good and...

00:17:46.566 --> 00:17:48.359
What the hell?!

00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:51.905
That's for adding another tree

00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:51.905
to  One Tree Hill!

00:17:51.947 --> 00:17:54.365
Oh, my God, he destroyed

00:17:51.947 --> 00:17:54.365
every last box!

00:17:54.407 --> 00:17:55.492
Holy crap!

00:17:55.533 --> 00:17:57.076
We're sunk now, Peter.

00:17:57.118 --> 00:18:00.455
There goes your one chance to

00:17:57.118 --> 00:18:00.455
get TV back to the way it was.

00:18:00.497 --> 00:18:02.373
Wait a minute.

00:18:00.497 --> 00:18:02.373
Maybe not, Brian.

00:18:02.415 --> 00:18:04.960
I think I just got an idea.

00:18:05.002 --> 00:18:06.878
Aah!

00:18:05.002 --> 00:18:06.878
I got glass in my face!

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:09.464
Oh, crap.

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:09.464
Now I forgot what it was.

00:18:09.506 --> 00:18:10.465
I got it!

00:18:10.507 --> 00:18:12.009
Aah! Son of a bitch!

00:18:15.553 --> 00:18:16.471
You know who I hate?

00:18:16.513 --> 00:18:17.430
The troops.

00:18:17.472 --> 00:18:18.849
Yeah, me, too.

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:20.517
Whoa, whoa, whoa,

00:18:18.890 --> 00:18:20.517
who are you?

00:18:20.558 --> 00:18:21.559
I'm Peter Griffin.

00:18:21.601 --> 00:18:22.602
I'm the guy

00:18:21.601 --> 00:18:22.602
who ruined television,

00:18:22.644 --> 00:18:24.354
and I'm the guy

00:18:22.644 --> 00:18:24.354
who's gonna fix it.

00:18:24.395 --> 00:18:25.355
Guys!

00:18:25.396 --> 00:18:26.356
I broke television,

00:18:26.397 --> 00:18:28.107
and now you have

00:18:26.397 --> 00:18:28.107
to help me fix it!

00:18:28.149 --> 00:18:29.192
Yah-ha!

00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:31.486
Looks like this is one

00:18:29.233 --> 00:18:31.486
we beat you to.

00:18:35.532 --> 00:18:37.034
Gentlemen, I have

00:18:35.532 --> 00:18:37.034
gathered you all here today

00:18:37.075 --> 00:18:39.995
because you are the creators

00:18:37.075 --> 00:18:39.995
of what television used to be

00:18:40.037 --> 00:18:41.412
before I ruined it.

00:18:41.454 --> 00:18:43.915
And we need to rebuild

00:18:41.454 --> 00:18:43.915
television from the ground up.

00:18:43.957 --> 00:18:46.918
So, I'm gonna need

00:18:43.957 --> 00:18:46.918
all your best ideas.

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.796
J.J. Abrams, you take

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.796
wonder and complexity

00:18:49.838 --> 00:18:51.882
and present it in a way that

00:18:49.838 --> 00:18:51.882
no one can possibly understand.

00:18:51.923 --> 00:18:53.050
Whaddaya got?!

00:18:53.091 --> 00:18:54.551
I've got an alien

00:18:53.091 --> 00:18:54.551
that goes back in time

00:18:54.592 --> 00:18:58.013
and encounters a koala bear

00:18:54.592 --> 00:18:58.013
in an Eastern European town.

00:18:58.055 --> 00:18:59.389
Totally confused.

00:18:58.055 --> 00:18:59.389
Do it!

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:01.933
Okay, now, we're gonna need

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:01.933
15 workplace comedies

00:19:01.975 --> 00:19:04.143
where people talk

00:19:01.975 --> 00:19:04.143
to the camera for some reason.

00:19:04.185 --> 00:19:06.270
You, you, you and you-- go.

00:19:06.938 --> 00:19:08.398
When Peter told me to make

00:19:08.439 --> 00:19:09.816
a workplace comedy

00:19:08.439 --> 00:19:09.816
where people talk

00:19:09.858 --> 00:19:10.734
to the camera, I thought...

00:19:10.775 --> 00:19:12.736
Not now!

00:19:10.775 --> 00:19:12.736
I mean, go do a show!

00:19:12.777 --> 00:19:14.946
Don't-don't do

00:19:12.777 --> 00:19:14.946
that thing here.

00:19:14.988 --> 00:19:16.031
Huh.

00:19:16.073 --> 00:19:17.407
Wonder if I can

00:19:16.073 --> 00:19:17.407
pull off one of those

00:19:17.448 --> 00:19:19.409
"can you believe what

00:19:17.448 --> 00:19:19.409
I have to put up with" looks

00:19:19.450 --> 00:19:21.036
to the camera.

00:19:23.788 --> 00:19:26.499
Okay, Mark Burnett, you did

00:19:23.788 --> 00:19:26.499
Survivor and  The Apprentice.

00:19:26.541 --> 00:19:29.460
Can you give me a reality show

00:19:26.541 --> 00:19:29.460
where people do horrible,

00:19:29.502 --> 00:19:30.587
unforgiveable things

00:19:29.502 --> 00:19:30.587
to each other

00:19:30.628 --> 00:19:32.380
for embarrassingly

00:19:30.628 --> 00:19:32.380
small sums of money?

00:19:32.422 --> 00:19:33.464
I got some ideas.

00:19:33.506 --> 00:19:36.384
Here's a nickel,

00:19:33.506 --> 00:19:36.384
pull down your pants.

00:19:36.426 --> 00:19:37.635
There's a show.

00:19:37.677 --> 00:19:39.137
Yah-ha! Go!

00:19:40.597 --> 00:19:41.556
All right, now,

00:19:40.597 --> 00:19:41.556
who's gonna make a show

00:19:41.598 --> 00:19:42.473
about horrible

00:19:41.598 --> 00:19:42.473
New Jersey freaks?

00:19:42.515 --> 00:19:43.141
You know what?

00:19:42.515 --> 00:19:43.141
I don't care.

00:19:43.182 --> 00:19:45.268
Just someone, do it!

00:19:46.103 --> 00:19:47.228
Okay, Dick Wolf,

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:49.564
make the same  Law and Order

00:19:47.270 --> 00:19:49.564
six times.

00:19:49.606 --> 00:19:51.441
Oh, and also,

00:19:49.606 --> 00:19:51.441
could you marry Matt Weiner

00:19:51.482 --> 00:19:53.443
'cause I want your name

00:19:51.482 --> 00:19:53.443
to be Dick "Weener."

00:19:53.484 --> 00:19:55.653
Okay, but can I go by

00:19:53.484 --> 00:19:55.653
"Dick Wolf-Weener"?

00:19:55.695 --> 00:19:57.614
Oh, my God, yes!

00:19:55.695 --> 00:19:57.614
Yes! Yes!

00:19:57.655 --> 00:19:59.032
Okay, Bravo people,

00:19:57.655 --> 00:19:59.032
go find women fighting.

00:19:59.074 --> 00:20:00.617
No, you know what,

00:19:59.074 --> 00:20:00.617
just find women.

00:20:00.658 --> 00:20:01.993
They'll end up fighting.

00:20:02.035 --> 00:20:04.579
All right, everyone who's left,

00:20:02.035 --> 00:20:04.579
make a talent show.

00:20:04.621 --> 00:20:05.956
We are done.

00:20:05.997 --> 00:20:09.500
Oh, Kelsey Grammer,

00:20:05.997 --> 00:20:09.500
what are you still doing here?

00:20:09.542 --> 00:20:10.794
I-I have nothing left

00:20:09.542 --> 00:20:10.794
for you.

00:20:10.835 --> 00:20:12.045
I'm... I'm sorry.

00:20:12.087 --> 00:20:15.590
Ah. Then I shall take

00:20:12.087 --> 00:20:15.590
my ease on the lanai.

00:20:15.632 --> 00:20:17.383
I don't care

00:20:15.632 --> 00:20:17.383
what you do now.

00:20:21.471 --> 00:20:23.848
TV ANNOUNCER: We now return

00:20:21.471 --> 00:20:23.848
to  Mike and Molly.

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:25.683
Have you decided

00:20:23.890 --> 00:20:25.683
what you'd like to order?

00:20:25.725 --> 00:20:26.684
Yes, the chopped salad?

00:20:26.726 --> 00:20:28.895
I'll have everything

00:20:26.726 --> 00:20:28.895
except that.

00:20:28.937 --> 00:20:30.021
(studio audience laughing)

00:20:30.063 --> 00:20:30.855
(laughing)

00:20:30.897 --> 00:20:32.649
That waiter's like, "What?!"

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:33.441
Well, you did it, Peter.

00:20:33.483 --> 00:20:35.526
You got TV back to normal.

00:20:35.568 --> 00:20:37.654
Yeah, guys,

00:20:35.568 --> 00:20:37.654
I'm sorry for screwing up

00:20:37.695 --> 00:20:38.822
all your favorite shows.

00:20:38.863 --> 00:20:40.031
Ah, that's okay, Peter.

00:20:40.073 --> 00:20:41.032
So, what do you say?

00:20:41.074 --> 00:20:42.200
Are we pals again?

00:20:42.241 --> 00:20:44.119
Ah, course we are.

00:20:42.241 --> 00:20:44.119
You bet.

00:20:44.161 --> 00:20:45.620
Well, let's drink

00:20:44.161 --> 00:20:45.620
to having TV

00:20:45.662 --> 00:20:48.665
back in the hands of people

00:20:45.662 --> 00:20:48.665
who know what they're doing.

00:20:48.706 --> 00:20:50.541
I think  Zack and Cody

00:20:48.706 --> 00:20:50.541
would be funnier

00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:52.543
if they did the show

00:20:50.583 --> 00:20:52.543
in their underpants.